# Pre-commit intentionally does NOT lint, validate filenames, or check imports.
#
# lint-staged fanned eslint out over parallel chunks; on a loaded machine that
# was enough to get the chunks OOM-killed mid-commit, leaving a stale
# .git/index.lock behind and aborting the commit.
#
# Verification now happens ONCE: `npm run quality` is run in the foreground
# before pushing a batch, and authoritatively in CI — both of which cover
# lint, filenames, and forbidden imports. Commits stay cheap so work can be
# checkpointed often (see the incremental-commit rule) instead of being held
# hostage to a multi-minute hook. This hook is a deliberate no-op.
exit 0
